course: dictionary
lesson: 12679
title: Distribute: sharing things out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To distribute something means to give or share it out among a group of people. A teacher who hands a worksheet to every child is distributing worksheets. «The teacher distributed the books to the class.» The clue is that the books went to many children, not just one.
explain: Distribute can also mean to spread something over an area. «Distribute the seeds evenly across the soil» means scatter them so they are spread out, not in one heap. The word evenly is the clue: the seeds should be spread fairly and the same amount everywhere.
explain: In maths, distribute means to share a total into equal parts. «Distribute 12 sweets equally among 3 friends» tells you to make 3 equal groups, so each friend gets 4. Check your answer by swapping in your meaning: does sharing 12 sweets into 3 equal groups still make sense? Yes, so 4 is right.
fact: Distribute is a verb. Its forms are distribute, distributes, distributed and distributing.
fact: «Distribute» means to give or share things out among a number of people.
fact: «Distribute» can also mean to spread something over an area, as in «distribute the seeds evenly».
fact: In maths, «distribute equally» means to divide a total into equal shares.
fact: The distributive law says 3 × (4 + 5) = 3 × 4 + 3 × 5. Both sides equal 27.
exercise: «The teacher distributed the worksheets to every child.» What does distributed mean here? | Threw them away | *Gave out, sharing them among the class | Hid them in a drawer | Counted them only
exercise: «Distribute 12 sweets equally among 3 friends.» How many sweets does each friend get? | 36 | 3 | 9 | *4
exercise: «Distribute the seeds evenly across the field.» Which word tells you the seeds should be spread fairly and the same everywhere? | Seeds | *Evenly | Field | Across the sky
test: «The charity will distribute food to the families in the village.» What does distribute mean here? | To count the food | To cook the food | *Give out to people who need it | To hide the food
test: Which statement shows the distributive law? | 3 + 4 + 5 = 12 | 4 + 3 = 3 + 4 | 3 × 4 × 5 = 60 | *3 × (4 + 5) = 3 × 4 + 3 × 5
exam: Aisha has 20 stickers to distribute equally among 4 children. How many stickers does each child get? | 4 | 16 | *5 | 24
